    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "All external facing materials, treatments and finishes shall be similar to those of the original building and maintained and retained thereafter. This applies unless differences are shown on the drawings we have approved. \r\rReason: To ensure that the extension harmonises with the existing building and to ensure compliance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Fire Safety Statement.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12.",
    "The air source heat pumps shall only operate between 0600hrs and 1700hrs and no other time as assessed and stated in the Acoustic impact assessment reference: 8088_001R_1-0_RHM.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbours in accordance with policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018, by minimising impacts of the development that would otherwise give rise to nuisance.",
    "Before commencement of operation of the Air Source Heat Pumps an acoustic enclosure shall be installed around the air source heat pumps as specified in 5.70 & 5.71 of the submitted acoustic impact assessment report reference: 8088_001R_1-0_RHM.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbours in accordance with policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018, by minimising impacts of the development that would otherwise give rise to nuisance."
